schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: "COVID-19 disrupted over 80% of concentrated meat-processing production"
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    When COVID-19 shut down a handful of major meat-processing plants, over
    80 percent of production was disrupted and millions of people felt the
    impact — used as the article's example of centralized food distribution's
    single-point-of-failure weakness.
  evidence: >-
    Stated as fact in the article's "What Are Centralized Systems?" section;
    the article's References list only Bankless Academy and the PMC 2022
    study generally, with no specific inline citation tied to this 80%
    figure.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/centralized-vs-decentralized.md
  interpretation: >-
    Used as the concrete real-world illustration of "single point of
    failure": concentrating production in a small number of large
    facilities means one disruption cascades widely.
  uncertainty: >-
    The specific "over 80 percent" figure has no dedicated citation in the
    article itself (unlike the article's other major claim, which is tied
    to the named 2022 PMC study) — treat as an uncited statistic pending
    verification against a primary source (e.g. USDA or CDC COVID-19 meat-
    processing disruption reporting).
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/centralized-vs-decentralized.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-a42af3f6559f
